# biahub pins cytoland to a git commit via [tool.uv.sources], which pip-compile cannot read,
# and cytoland is not published on PyPI. Mirror that source here so pip-compile can resolve it.
# cytoland depends on the viscy-* workspace packages from the same VisCy repo (also not on
# PyPI), so each must be listed explicitly too. Keep this rev in sync with biahub's
# [tool.uv.sources] entry for cytoland.
